CFG692: gravitating polarization - the bound charge div P of a vacuum polarization field as the cold mass.

Criteria: FROZEN_CRITERIA.md (committed alone, 097b2feee). Units: u = 4 pi G |P| (an acceleration).
W(P) = 2 pi G P^2 + (4 pi G)^2 P^3/(3 a0)  =>  W'(P) = u + u^2/a0 (critical medium + SI cubic). Antiscreening: g = g_N + u.
kappa = 1/2 FITTED; footings never pooled; the cold energy's mass is required; no particle species; not "theory closed".

Run:  OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 nice -n 10 python3 cfg692.py      (CFG692_MUTATE=1: off-critical, screening sign, nu = 1; exit 1 iff all bite)

T1  static law: W'(P) = g and g = g_N + sign*u
    u(g) = sqrt(a_0)*sqrt(a_0 + 4*g)/2 - a_0/2;  g_N(g) = -sqrt(a_0)*sqrt(a_0 + 4*g)/2 + a_0/2 + g;  mu(x = g/a0) = (2*x - sqrt(4*x + 1) + 1)/(2*x)
    deep: lim g->0 g_N/(g^2/a0) = 1;  Newtonian: lim g->oo mu = 1;  high-field u ~ 1 sqrt(a0 g)
  [PASS] T1 deep g_N = g^2/a0 and mu -> 1: deep ratio 1, mu(oo) 1
    inverse g(g_N): [-sqrt(a_0)*sqrt(g_N) + g_N, sqrt(a_0)*sqrt(g_N) + g_N]
    equals g_N + sqrt(a0 g_N) (nu = 1 + y^-1/2, the CFG690 interpolation): True

T2  second variation per mode: Q = diag(W'', W'/P) - 4 pi G khat khat^T  (+ gamma k^2 I); khat = (c, s), c^2 + s^2 = 1
    W'' = 4*pi*G*(a_0 + 2*u)/a_0;  W'/P = 4*pi*G*(a_0 + u)/a_0;  longitudinal margin W'' - 4piG = 8*pi*G*u/a_0;  transverse-with-k-along-dP margin = 4*pi*G*u/a_0
    PD condition (gamma = 0): c^2/(W''/4piG) + s^2/((W'/P)/4piG) = a_0*(a_0 - c**2*u + 2*u)/(a_0**2 + 3*a_0*u + 2*u**2) < 1
  [PASS] T2 static medium stable for every P > 0 at gamma = 0: max PD condition over u/a0 in {1e-4..1e2}, all k directions = 0.999900 (< 1); longitudinal margin 8*pi*G*u/a_0
    deep regime (u << a0): margins -> 0 as u/a0 -> 0 (the medium is near-critical there; restoring rate ~ sqrt(8 pi G u/(a0 I)))

T3  (a) Poisson: lap Phi = 4 pi G (rho_b + div P): the cold mass rho_c = div P is in the one equation that sets the metric
    (b) deep spherical: P = sqrt(M)*sqrt(a_0)/(4*pi*sqrt(G)*r);  rho_c = div P = sqrt(M)*sqrt(a_0)/(4*pi*sqrt(G)*r**2);  M_c(<r) = surface flux 4 pi r^2 P = sqrt(M)*sqrt(a_0)*r/sqrt(G) (= volume integral sqrt(M)*sqrt(a_0)*r/sqrt(G))
  [PASS] T3 deep cold mass rho_c ~ r^-2, M_c(<r) ~ r, M_c = surface flux (moved, not created): the compensating negative bound charge sits where P falls to zero: the outer edge of each polarized region

